<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Purnananda Burhagohain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1817">1817</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Purnananda <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burhagohain">Burhagohain</a> was chief minister (Burhagohain) of the Ahom kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> from 1784 to 1817 and its effective ruler for much of that time. He suppressed the last Moamoria resistance, restored much of the state after the rebellion and installed the kings Kamaleswar Singha and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandrakanta-singha">Chandrakanta Singha</a>. The appeal of his rivals to the Burmese court led to the invasions that ended Ahom independence.</p></div>
